// `full`'s colours (colorization Step 9; data since sprite editor Step 1),
// chosen by eye from Samus Returns screenshots and James's direction: each
// Metroid II area after its paired Samus Returns area (`docs/colorization.md`,
// "The colours"). `colors.zig` imports this file at compile time.
//
// Every colour is 0xRRGGBB as the SNES shows it: a BGR555 colour with each
// 5-bit channel `c` written `(c << 3) | (c >> 2)` (`colors.rgb888`), so the
// file says exactly what the cart draws. A table is four shades, lightest
// first, indexed like the Game Boy's: shade 3 is black.
//
// An object palette (`obj`, `damage`, `suits`) is four such tables: its
// variants (sprite editor Step 2). A sprite pixel's colour index `i` (1-15,
// never 4, 8 or 12) is shade `i & 3` through OBP0 `$93` of variant `i >> 2`,
// so variant 0 is what the Game Boy's art shows and the others are colours an
// edited tile may use instead. An unedited variant repeats variant 0. Shade 3
// of every variant is never drawn (it is colour 0, 4, 8 or 12) and stays
// black.
//
// This file is maintained by hand and by the sprite editor, which patches
// values in place and leaves the comments alone.
.{
    // Each colour set's BG3 palettes (`areas.setOf`): the areas in id order,
    // then their `nest` variants, then `acid` and `bubbles`. A slot is the
    // same kind of thing in every set: 0 the main rock, 2 the second rock, 4
    // machinery (the ship, the ruins' insides), 6 a second structure (the
    // bubbles), 7 the plants. Slots 1, 3 and 5 hold the tiles drawn the same
    // everywhere (`full_assign.tile_choices`): spikes and coral red, the
    // liquid that slows Samus yellow, acid purple. Every BG slot's shade 3 is
    // black: BGP `$93` puts it at colour 0, the backdrop.
    .bg = .{
        // 0: surface (Samus Returns' surface): amber rock, chartreuse, the gunship
        .{
            .{ 0xDEBD94, 0xC68431, 0x422910, 0x000000 }, // 0: main rock
            .{ 0xF78C8C, 0xF71818, 0x520808, 0x000000 }, // 1: spikes and coral (red)
            .{ 0xC6D694, 0x8CAD31, 0x313910, 0x000000 }, // 2: second rock
            .{ 0xEFDE94, 0xE7C631, 0x4A4210, 0x000000 }, // 3: slowing liquid (yellow)
            .{ 0xF7CE94, 0xEF9C29, 0x523108, 0x000000 }, // 4: machinery
            .{ 0xC694E7, 0x9429D6, 0x31084A, 0x000000 }, // 5: acid (purple)
            .{ 0xB5C694, 0x6B8C29, 0x213108, 0x000000 }, // 6: second structure
            .{ 0xE7B5A5, 0xD66B4A, 0x4A2118, 0x000000 }, // 7: plants
        },
